<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Flutter on TECH-ANDGAR</title><link>https://tech-andgar.me/categories/flutter/</link><description>Recent content in Flutter on TECH-ANDGAR</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 07 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://tech-andgar.me/categories/flutter/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>A Comprehensive Guide to Flutter Widget Previews (Beta)</title><link>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/flutter-widget-previews-guide/</link><pubDate>Fri, 07 Nov 2025 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/flutter-widget-previews-guide/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="overview"&gt;
 Overview
 &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#overview"&gt;
 &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
 &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Flutter Widget Previews is a powerful experimental feature that allows developers to see widgets render in real-time, separate from a full app, in the Chrome browser. This guide covers how to implement, run, and optimize widget previews in Flutter applications. It is designed to complement the &lt;a href="https://docs.flutter.dev/tools/widget-previewer" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;official Flutter documentation on the Widget Previewer&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id="understanding-the-beta-status"&gt;
 Understanding the &amp;lsquo;Beta&amp;rsquo; Status
 &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#understanding-the-beta-status"&gt;
 &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
 &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It is crucial to understand what &amp;ldquo;Beta&amp;rdquo; and &amp;ldquo;Experimental&amp;rdquo; mean in a practical sense for your team&amp;rsquo;s workflow.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Solving Artifacts with `ImageFilter.blur` in Flutter on Android, iOS and macOS</title><link>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/solving-artifacts-imagefilter-blur-flutter/</link><pubDate>Sun, 27 Oct 2024 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/solving-artifacts-imagefilter-blur-flutter/</guid><description>&lt;h1 id="solving-artifacts-with-imagefilterblur-in-flutter-on-android-ios-and-macos"&gt;
 Solving Artifacts with &lt;code&gt;ImageFilter.blur&lt;/code&gt; in Flutter on Android, iOS and macOS
 &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#solving-artifacts-with-imagefilterblur-in-flutter-on-android-ios-and-macos"&gt;
 &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
 &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://github.com/flutter/flutter/issues/157693" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;&lt;img src="https://tech-andgar.me/posts/solving-artifacts-imagefilter-blur-flutter/preview-issue.webp" alt="Flutter ImageFilter.blur Issue"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="introduction"&gt;
 Introduction
 &lt;a class="heading-link" href="#introduction"&gt;
 &lt;i class="fa-solid fa-link" aria-hidden="true" title="Link to heading"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;
 &lt;span class="sr-only"&gt;Link to heading&lt;/span&gt;
 &lt;/a&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When developing mobile and desktop applications with Flutter, it&amp;rsquo;s common to use blur effects to enhance the user interface. One of the most used methods is &lt;code&gt;ImageFilter.blur&lt;/code&gt;. However, some developers have encountered visual artifacts when applying this effect on Android, iOS and macOS, while it works correctly on web. In this article, we&amp;rsquo;ll explore this issue, understand the reason behind it, and provide an effective solution.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Flutter Test Coverage</title><link>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/flutter-test-coverage/</link><pubDate>Thu, 30 Sep 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://tech-andgar.me/posts/flutter-test-coverage/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;LCOV is a graphical tool for GCC coverage testing with gcov. It creates HTML pages containing source code annotated with coverage information by collecting gcov data from multiple source files. LCOV supports &amp;ldquo;Line Coverage&amp;rdquo; and &amp;ldquo;Function Coverage&amp;rdquo; measurement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The LCOV report looks as follows:&lt;/p&gt;
